# macOS noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Bun + Node (future-proof for when SPEC-001 build kicks off)
# NOTE: build/ is anchored to the repo root so it only ignores a root-level
# build-output dir, NOT the skills/build/ lifecycle-skill source.
node_modules/
dist/
/build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Packaging output: staging tarballs of the skills tree (e.g. _stage_skills.tgz).
# Derived snapshots, regenerable from the tree they were cut from. Unanchored
# because no archive is ever source here — nothing under skills/ ships as a .tgz.
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Test output
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Scratch: run artifacts from the docs-tree verification tools (impact
# manifests, closure reports, reconcile and figure reports, capability
# surveys). Anchored to the repo root so a skills/**/scratch/ source dir would
# not be caught.
#
# Ignored rather than committed because every file in here is DERIVED and
# cheap to regenerate — each is the output of a read-only tool run against a
# graph that moves independently of this repo. Committing them would freeze a
# point-in-time census next to the code that produces it, and a stale manifest
# read as current is worse than no manifest. A run worth keeping belongs in the
# knowledge graph as a note, not here.
# Written as `/scratch/*` rather than `/scratch/` so the exception below can
# apply: git never descends into an excluded directory, so a negation inside one
# is silently dead. Excluding the CONTENTS keeps the directory traversable.
/scratch/*

# Exception: the consolidation programme's prompts are NOT derived artifacts.
# `prompts-v2/` carries the owner's rulings in his own quoted words, the run
# contract, and the twelve authored prompts that drive the programme. None of it
# regenerates from a tool run — losing it loses the decisions themselves — and
# each edit to a ruling is exactly the kind of change that wants a reviewable
# diff. Tracked for history and recovery; the rest of scratch/ stays ignored.
!/scratch/prompts-v2/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
bun-debug.log*

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS noise (Windows + Linux)
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# plugin build output — generated, never committed
plugin/dist/
